<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt27" typeof="mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Group testing"}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwkA"><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1368532237" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt28" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'>.mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output div.hatnote{padding-left:1.6em;margin-bottom:0.5em}.mw-parser-output .hatnote i{font-style:normal}.mw-parser-output .hatnote+.mw-empty-elt+.hatnote{margin-top:-0.5em}@media print{body.ns-0 .mw-parser-output .hatnote{display:none!important}}</style></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt27" id="mwkQ">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Group_testing" title="Group testing">Group testing</a></div>
<p id="mwkg">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Non-adaptive_group_testing" title="Non-adaptive group testing" class="mw-redirect" id="mwkw">non-adaptive group testing</a> problem postulates that we have a test which can tell us, for any set of items, whether that set contains a <i id="mwlA">defective</i> item. We are asked to come up with a series of groupings that can exactly identify all the defective items in a batch of <i id="mwlQ">n</i> total items, some <i id="mwlg">d</i> of which are defective.</p>

<p id="mwlw">A <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt29" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"d"}}' id="mwmA"><span class="mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle d}">
  <semantics>
